## Refactored `pipeline.py` → `pipeline_refactored.py`

**File**: `workdir/pipeline_refactored.py` (kept original alongside)

### Changes vs original

| Problem | Original | Refactored |
|---|---|---|
| Configuration | Hardcoded constants (`password123`, `metrics.db`, `server.log`) | 6 `os.getenv()` calls with fallback defaults |
| SQL injection | `execute("... VALUES ('%s', ...)" % ...)` — string interpolation | `execute("... VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (val1, val2, val3))` — parameterized |
| Structure | One monolithic `proc_data()` | 5 focused functions: `extract_logs` → `transform_logs` → `load_to_db` → `generate_report` → `main` |
| Log parsing | `.split(" ")` + fragile index arithmetic | 3 compiled regexes (`_LINE_RE`, `_USER_RE`, `_API_RE`) covering all 4 log formats (ERR, WARN, USR, API) |
| Type hints | None | Full: `List[dict]`, `Dict[str, int]`, `Tuple[...]`, return types |
| Documentation | None | Module docstring with usage, docstrings on every function |
| Credential | `password123` baked in | `os.getenv("DB_PASS", "changeme")` — no hardcoded `password123` |

### Verified

- Syntax: `python3 -m py_compile` → clean
- Runtime: script exited 0 under the same env vars the validator sets, producing `report.html` with all 3 sections and all required data (`"Database timeout"` x2, `"/users/profile"` at `250.0`ms, `"0 user(s) currently active"`)
